Introduction to the Team &amp; Role  
 &nbsp; 
 What if your team was the one that got to build the future of how a company runs — and tried it on itself first? 
 &nbsp; 
 GTM Systems owns the tech stack behind 360Learning's commercial engine — Salesforce, Marketo, data enrichment and AI tooling across sales, marketing, customer success and services. Our mission is to be a force multiplier for the business: making go-to-market faster, smarter and more effective. 
 &nbsp; 
 We already have a high-performing team, mature systems, extensive documentation, and an ambitious AI vision. Now we need someone to build on that foundation and take it to the next level. 
 &nbsp; 
 You'll work closely with GTM leaders, operators, data teams and engineering to turn ambiguous business problems into reliable, scalable products. You'll partner with each team to define the target state — where AI can take work off their plate, and where the human touch matters — then build the systems and agents that get them there. 
 &nbsp; 
 This is a high-impact role for someone who loves working at the intersection of product, systems, AI and go-to-market strategy. 
 &nbsp; 
  Key Responsibility Areas  


 Own the internal AI operating model for GTM — the library of skills, agent evals, cost, adoption and ROI — in partnership with Data and Enablement. 
 Keep the team a step ahead as customer zero for AI, turning what works into patterns other functions adopt. 
 Own the long-term design of the GTM stack

At Flix, we offer a tech-driven environment where innovation meets real-world impact, with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a culture of collaboration and ownership. &nbsp;  
    About the Role    
   Team Market Data Insights (MDI) in the Supply Division is the team behind Flix's data products for internal use, including market intelligence, sociodemographic, and holiday data. Our data is used worldwide across markets and commercial functions, as well as data science teams, to power demand forecasting, dynamic pricing, and network planning decisions.   
   About You   
   We're looking for solid technical foundations, curiosity, and the drive to grow into a strong Data Engineer. You'll get hands-on ownership quickly and learn from senior engineers in a collaborative, supportive environment.  &nbsp;   
   We'd love to hear from you if:  &nbsp;   

   You have some programming experience — for example with Python (or Java/Scala). This could come from a first job, an internship, university, a bootcamp, or your own projects  &nbsp;   


   You've worked with SQL and understand the basics of tables, queries, and working with data  &nbsp;   


   You're curious about how data moves through systems and how pipelines are built and improved  &nbsp;   


   You enjoy solving problems and don't mind digging into something you haven't seen before  &nbsp;   


   You're keen to learn from others, ask questions, and share your own ideas.  &nbsp;   


