description_html:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*This position is fully remote/home based. Applications will be accepted from candidates based in the UK and the following US states: FL, IL, MA, MD, NY, PA, TX, VA.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director, Publishing provides strategic leadership for the PLOS journal portfolio, ensuring that portfolio priorities, publishing investments, and journal development strategies align with organizational goals and advance PLOS&#39;s mission.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Director, Publishing &amp;amp; Publishing Operations, the Associate Director leads and develops a team of Publishers responsible for the performance and strategic development of journals portfolios. The Associate Director serves as the primary steward of portfolio-wide publishing performance, translating organizational strategy into clear priorities and ensuring effective coordination across the organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director uses publishing data, financial information, market intelligence, and research community insight to guide strategic decisions, establish priorities, identify opportunities for growth and innovation, and manage risks. Working in partnership with the Director, Publishing &amp;amp; Publishing Operations, the Associate Director ensures that journal-level strategies collectively support a sustainable PLOS portfolio with a strong value proposition.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supervisory Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and support a team of senior publishing professionals responsible for journal and subject portfolio performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear goals, priorities, and measures of accountability that align with organizational and portfolio strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching, professional development, succession planning, and performance management for direct reports.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of collaboration, inclusion, accountability, innovation, and continuous improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Publishers to ensure effective leadership and development of Journal Development Managers and other publishing staff.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Portfolio Strategy and Performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement a portfolio-wide publishing strategy aligned with PLOS&#39;s mission and organizational objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that journal and subject portfolio strategies collectively support a clear and differentiated value proposition for the PLOS portfolio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regular portfolio reviews and develop recommendations regarding journal positioning, growth opportunities, performance, and future direction.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance the needs of individual journals and research communities with broader portfolio and organizational objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Publishers in identifying and responding to changes in research communities, funding policies, scholarly communication, and the publishing market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop consistent approaches and decision-making frameworks for evaluating proposals, opportunities, and performance across the portfolio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the evaluation and development of new journals, products, services, publishing models in line with PLOS’s strategic direction.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic and Business Leadership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate organizational strategy into clear portfolio priorities, objectives, and plans for the publishing team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee publishing budgets and forecasts in partnership with the Director and Publishers, ensuring responsible decision-making and effective resource allocation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a thought partner to, and deputize for, the Director, Publishing &amp;amp; Publishing Operations when appropriate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In close collaboration with colleagues in Editorial, Sales and Global Publishing Development, support publishers in developing impactful relationships with Editors-in-Chief, Editorial Board members, researchers, institutions, societies, and partner organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build productive partnerships across Editorial, Publishing Operations, Sales &amp;amp; Global Publishing Development, Product, Technology, Marketing, Finance, Research Integrity, and other organizational teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Editorial and Publishing Operations leaders to ensure that journal strategies are supported by effective policies, processes, services, and quality standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing and Communications to strengthen journal positioning, audience engagement, portfolio visibility, and demand generation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Leadership and Culture&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model the culture and behaviors PLOS is seeking to build, actively driving the culture change the organization needs through this transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a collaborative leader across PLOS, fostering strong cross-functional partnerships and organizational alignment that enable shared organizational priorities to be delivered successfully.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead change effectively by ensuring a clear strategic rationale, defined outcomes, appropriate measures of success, realistic resource requirements and clear accountability and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business problem solver – operates with curiosity to get to the root of the business problem to ensure the ultimate solution is grounded in PLOS’s strategy and mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience launching Open Access journals from proposal to publication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and financial skills, including experience with budgeting, forecasting, business planning and P&amp;amp;L ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience in STM publishing with progressively increased responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing senior publishing professionals, or comparable portfolio leaders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop and execute strategic plans that deliver measurable business and operational outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of leading and developing high-performing, geographically distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, relationship-building, and stakeholder management skills across cultures, disciplines, and organizational functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedication to open access and transforming scholarly communication, with a genuine interest in engaging productively with the scientific community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading high-volume journal portfolios and/or megajournals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements and Work Environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prolonged periods stationary at a desk and working on a computer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some national and international travel may be required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some flexibility to work across time zones may be required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range we’ve established for these positions is (&lt;strong&gt;US): $145,000- $157,000 or (UK) £90,000- £104,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;PLOS also offers a comprehensive benefits package summarized below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;BENEFITS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee sponsored health, dental and vision insurance (Dental and Vision 100% employer paid)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Vacation, 11 public holidays and sick leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Birthday and three winter holidays days off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short term and long term disability insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 days paid time off for volunteering per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote work environment with stipend on joining for home office&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;UK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Private medical insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Life assurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Income protection &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Personal accident insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Pension with up to 10% employer match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;25 days holidays, market competitive Maternity and Paternity leave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Birthday and three winter holidays days off&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;2 days paid time off for volunteering per year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;Fully remote work environment with stipend on joining for home office&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About PLOS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building on a strong legacy of pioneering innovation, PLOS continues to be a catalyst in open science, reimagining models to meet open science principles, removing barriers and promoting inclusion in knowledge creation and sharing, and publishing research outputs that enable everyone to learn from, reuse and build upon scientific knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work is supported by a highly skilled global in-house team, partnerships with local scholarly organizations, and the valued contributions of a diverse, international community of scientific researchers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re committed to equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re working to create a more equitable system of scientific knowledge and understanding. Removing barriers to inclusion and facilitating broad participation of voices is core to our success, inside and out.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond accepting distinct perspectives, we seek and support divergent backgrounds among our staff because we know differences strengthen our teams, our work, and our communities. We strongly encourage applicants of all identities to join us as we work towards a future where science is open to all, for all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;http://plos.org/careers&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;plos.org/careers&lt;/a&gt; to learn more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To learn more about how PLOS protects your privacy, see our &lt;a href=&quot;https://plos.org/employee-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Employee Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

